       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. The usual adult starting dose is 5 mg, or 2.5 mg for frail patients. A dose of 50 mg could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because of amlodipine's long half-life, those effects can last for days.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the standard starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n\nIf 50 mg is what you intend, please confirm and tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though I'd strongly suggest discussing it with pharmacy first.\n\nOnce you tell me the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
